WEBVTT

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.783
and I worked as a community organizer
and on a congressional campaign.

00:01:32.178 --> 00:01:34.828
CQ: So as Lauran and I
were getting to know each other,

00:01:34.852 --> 00:01:37.775
it was right in the middle
of that 2012 presidential campaign,

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:40.292
and most of our early
political conversations

00:01:40.316 --> 00:01:42.831
were really just based
in jokes and pranks.

00:01:43.244 --> 00:01:46.276
So as an example, I would change
Lauran's computer screen saver

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.729
to a picture of Mitt Romney,

00:01:47.753 --> 00:01:51.150
or she would put an Obama
campaign magnet on the back of my car.

00:01:51.174 --> 00:01:52.185
(Laughter)

00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:54.249
LA: Car, not minivan.

00:01:54.273 --> 00:01:57.281
CQ: But over time,
those conversations grew more serious

00:01:57.305 --> 00:01:59.964
and really became
a core of our friendship.

00:01:59.988 --> 00:02:01.406
And somewhere along the line,